WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.065
The web was built to share pages.

00:00:03.105 --> 00:00:05.087
What if it could share agents?

00:00:06.437 --> 00:00:08.877
WebAgentica separates three roles.

00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:12.005
AgentStudio creates a portable agent package.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.911
AgentHosting publishes it.

00:00:13.951 --> 00:00:17.511
AgentSurfer downloads it, and runs it in your browser.

00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:19.585
Jane wants to book a flight.

00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:21.089
She visits WebAir.

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:24.794
Instead of navigating pages, she clicks Open Agent.

00:00:25.144 --> 00:00:28.518
WebAir's agent package downloads to Jane's computer.

00:00:28.558 --> 00:00:30.833
Her AgentSurfer browser verifies it,

00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:34.762
then runs it in a sandbox, inside AgentVM.

00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:38.640
The agent helps Jane search flights, using her chosen model,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.954
her memory, and only the permissions she grants.

00:00:42.304 --> 00:00:46.073
The same AgentVM runs agents from other websites too,

00:00:46.113 --> 00:00:50.683
like travel insurance or a hotel, each in its own sandbox.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.313
Websites no longer just serve pages.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:56.046
They can serve downloadable AI agents.

00:00:56.086 --> 00:00:58.710
Your AgentSurfer browser runs them locally,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.666
using the same AgentVM across different websites.

00:01:03.016 --> 00:01:04.326
WebAgentica.

00:01:04.366 --> 00:01:05.509
Create anywhere.

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:06.683
Host anywhere.

00:01:06.723 --> 00:01:08.158
Run anywhere.
